\begin{abstract}
The Autonomous Dark Domain Engine (ADDE-v4) is a unified computational
architecture for encrypted cosmological data ingestion, large-scale N-body
simulation, and dark-sector anomaly detection. The system combines
AMR+PM+Octree gravitational solvers with CKKS homomorphic encryption, enabling
privacy-preserving evaluation of lensing shear fields, BAO statistics, and
latent anomaly scores. We demonstrate numerical stability at
$16{,}384^3$ particle resolution, strong scaling efficiency of $78.6\%$, and
automated bootstrapping recovery at multiplicative depth~12. Stress tests under
$30\%$ intrinsic shape noise and $25\%$ masking yield convergence reconstructions
with $\mathrm{SNR}=8.42$, while Masked Autoregressive Flows detect injected
non-Gaussian perturbations at $5.12\sigma$. ADDE-v4 provides a validated
framework for real-time, privacy-preserving exploration of dark matter and dark
energy phenomenology in high-volume survey environments.
\end{abstract}